WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.399 --> 00:00:13.350
What sorts of activities can threaten the elements of the CIA Triad

2
00:00:18.139 --> 00:00:20.639
consider a coworker sharing passwords.

3
00:00:20.819 --> 00:00:24.809
Perhaps Joe gives Joanne his password because he is homesick and needs

4
00:00:24.819 --> 00:00:28.040
Joanne to sign into his work computer to get information he needs.

5
00:00:28.690 --> 00:00:31.469
But later, Joanne is fired from her job.

6
00:00:31.979 --> 00:00:34.950
The employer cancels Joanne's credentials but isn't

7
00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:37.770
aware that Joanne also knows Joe's password.

8
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.689
Joanne is disgruntled and decides to take revenge on her old

9
00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:45.860
company by using Joe's credentials to change or delete important files

10
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:48.509
or in less hostile circumstances.

11
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.950
Improper use of the password could accidentally result in the

12
00:00:51.959 --> 00:00:55.840
introduction of unauthorized software that is riddled with malware.

13
00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.830
Another example is the laptop of a remote worker

14
00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.869
being left unattended or unlocked in the worker's home.

15
00:01:03.509 --> 00:01:07.290
Children or other family members may decide to play games on the computer.

16
00:01:07.639 --> 00:01:11.010
They upload legal but contaminated software or files

17
00:01:11.019 --> 00:01:14.529
leading to a corrupt workstation with compromised integrity.

18
00:01:15.389 --> 00:01:17.940
The elements of the CIA triad can also be

19
00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:21.220
compromised by ill preparedness against acts of nature.

20
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:22.440
For instance,

21
00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.930
a long term power outage may lead to backup generators that run

22
00:01:25.940 --> 00:01:30.059
out of fuel or that suffer mechanical failures if not properly maintained

23
00:01:31.349 --> 00:01:32.959
as a final example,

24
00:01:33.059 --> 00:01:37.250
improper fire suppression methods can affect the CIA triad by

25
00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:41.209
irreparably damaging or destroying both digital and analog information.

26
00:01:42.230 --> 00:01:45.430
All these examples show that a comprehensive risk assessment

27
00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:49.779
of technical human and environmental threats must be completed,

28
00:01:50.029 --> 00:01:53.580
then appropriate mitigation options must be put in place to

29
00:01:53.589 --> 00:01:57.180
protect the security and integrity of an organization's information.